<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gurage people</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gurage are a people of south-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> living south-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/addis-ababa">Addis Ababa</a>, mainly in the Gurage Zone. They speak a group of Ethiopian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/semitic-languages">Semitic languages</a> and traditionally farm enset, the false banana. Their lands were incorporated into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menelik-ii">Menelik II</a> in the late 19th century, and many Gurage have since become traders and businesspeople in Addis Ababa and other towns.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gurage-people.jpg" alt="Gurage people" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gathering_infront_of_beautiful_traditional_gurage_house.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
